      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your exhaustion from constantly maintaining a mask is valid, and the feeling of being separated by an invisible wall by itself is incredibly isolating. It is a worthwhile struggle to finally let go of the need to pretend when the constant effort outweighs any potential reward. Please remember that asking for a moment to step back inside your own safety, away from all eyes and expectations, isn't weakness; it is a necessary space to heal that specific kind of deep bruising.",
      "source": "target",
