      "content": "This feeling of futility is exhausting, and it makes absolute sense to want the effort to stop when the outcome never feels achievable. You are not broken for wanting to conserve your strength because the \"game\" is rigged, and your desire to spend less energy justifying that outcome is a valid form of self-preservation. Sometimes, the only way to break the cycle isn't by trying harder, but by recognizing that your energy belongs to you, not to a story that no one else truly understands.",
